e-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.98639 -0.1644 0.1644 0.98639 151.35 161.78)"><path d="M 12.22 0 L 1.79 3.89 L 4.93 0 L 1.79 -3.89 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#008000;" color="#008000" stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 121.54 155.33 L 131.88 119.12"></path><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.27472 -0.96152 0.96152 0.27472 130.6 123.59)"><path d="M 12.22 0 L 1.79 3.89 L 4.93 0 L 1.79 -3.89 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" color="#0000FF" stroke-width="0.8pt"><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 182.75 168.64 L 226.6 256.34"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.4472 0.89442 -0.89442 0.4472 224.51 252.18)"><path d="M 12.22 0 L 1.79 3.89 L 4.93 0 L 1.79 -3.89 Z"></path></g></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" color="#0000FF" stroke-width="0.8pt"><g stroke-dasharray="3.0pt,3.0pt" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 128.56 90.03 L 110.41 73.53"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" color="#000000" stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-0.73994 -0.67267 0.67267 -0.73994 113.86 76.66)"><path d="M 12.22 0 L 1.79 3.89 L 4.93 0 L 1.79 -3.89 Z"></path></g></g></g></g></svg></span>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.sf1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="S4.F4.sf1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Illustration of an action that pushes the state (graph embedding) from known operating regions of the <span id="S4.F4.sf1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">grl</span> agent. In the illustrated scenario, from an initial state, the blue agent takes an action that causes the state of the network to transition to a new position in the latent space – see \raisebox{-0.9pt}{1}⃝. From here, assume that either a red or green action \raisebox{-0.9pt}{2}⃝, results in a transition to the state of the network such that the new state is outside the observed network topology data, \raisebox{-0.9pt}{3}⃝.</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<figure id="S4.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">
