</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Scaling to larger networks</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this experiment we scale the <span id="S5.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">cc2</span> network to have 1000 hosts across 10 subnets, with 100 hosts per subnet, across 50 episodes per red agent. <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is used for evaluation, results are shown in <a href="#S5.T2" title="In 5.3 Scaling to larger networks ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ General Autonomous Cybersecurity Defense:Learning Robust Policies for Dynamic Topologies and Diverse Attackers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S5.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Results for <math id="S5.T2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> when <span id="S5.T2.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">cc2</span> has been scaled significantly in size to have 1000 hosts across 10 different subnets. Evaluation is shown against two types of red-agent.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T2.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T2.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Red agent</th>
<th id="S5.T2.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Reward</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T2.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.6.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Meander</th>
<td id="S5.T2.6.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2.40\pm 5.65" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2.40</mn></mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>5.65</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2.40\pm 5.65</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T2.6.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T2.6.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">B-Line</th>
<td id="S5.T2.6.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><math id="S5.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-50.77\pm 20.45" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>50.77</mn></mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>20.45</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-50.77\pm 20.45</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As is evident in the Meander case, designing a good red agent on large networks is a difficult task. Even in the B-Line red agent setting, we only observe 23 impacts, i.e., a successful infection of the operational server, across 50 episodes, each of 100 steps.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Novel attack patterns</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next we explore novel attack patterns. We conduct two experiments where in the first, we retrain the <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">gacd</span> (<math id="S5.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) against only the B-Line agent and evaluate against the Meander red agent, and in the second experiment we train the <span id="S5.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">gacd</span> agent against the Meander red agent and evaluate against B-Line. <a href="#S5.T3" title="In 5.4 Novel attack patterns ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ General Autonomous Cybersecurity Defense:Learning Robust Policies for Dynamic Topologies and Diverse Attackers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> documents the observed performance.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="S5.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cross-evaluation performance between different red agent strategies.</span></figcaption>
<div id="S5.T3.5" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:46pt;vertical-align:-19.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(33.3pt,-4.4pt) scale(1.23902532585495,1.23902532585495) ;">
<table id="S5.T3.5.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T3.5.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T3.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Trained red agent</th>
<th id="S5.T3.5.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Evaluation red agent</th>
<th id="S5.T3.5.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">Reward</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T3.5.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T3.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">Meander</td>
<td id="S5.T3.5.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">B-Line</td>
<td id="S5.T3.5.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><math id="S5.T3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-15.93\pm 5.24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>15.93</mn></mrow><mo>±</mo><mn>5.24</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-15.93\pm 5.24</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
