<section id="S5.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.7 </span>Model adaptability to environment dynamics</h3>

<div id="S5.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the inference capability of the <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">gacd</span> agent by introducing a network topology change midway through an episode. The agent is trained on 8 topologies for <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\times 10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\times 10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math> timesteps, and during evaluation, the network shifts from the vanilla <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">cc2</span> topology to one of the trained topologies. Adaptability is assessed over 1000 episodes of 100 steps, with average rewards shown in <a href="#S5.F8" title="In 5.7 Model adaptability to environment dynamics ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ General Autonomous Cybersecurity Defense:Learning Robust Policies for Dynamic Topologies and Diverse Attackers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Compared to the <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">sota</span> <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ppo</span> agent, which becomes ineffective post-change (red curve, receiving the minimum reward of <math id="S5.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-3</annotation></semantics></math>), the <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">gacd</span> agent (black curve) adapts seamlessly with minimal reward degradation. We also evaluate a hybrid approach where a secondary <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ppo</span> agent is pre-trained on the new topology (blue curve). If the defense policy switches at the right moment, the combined <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ppo</span> agents perform comparably to a single <span id="S5.SS7.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">gacd</span> agent.</p>
</div>
