</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S5.F8.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="S5.F8.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of the averaged step-wise reward returned from a discontinuous environment for the <span id="S5.F8.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">gacd</span> agent vs the baseline <span id="S5.F8.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ppo</span> agent.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SS7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The results are available in tabular form in <a href="#S5.T6" title="In 5.7 Model adaptability to environment dynamics ‣ 5 Experiments ‣ General Autonomous Cybersecurity Defense:Learning Robust Policies for Dynamic Topologies and Diverse Attackers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, where we have also included comparison against one of the <span id="S5.SS7.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">mpnn</span> variations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table">
